                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Better than most of the other games in the series. Battles rely a lot more on tactics as opposed to taking advantage of the enemy AI like many missions in previous entries. Specifically I really enjoyed the Battle of Gilgal Church fighting as the Union,  where you have inflict 90% enemy casualties within a short amount of turns. The Confederates are heavily entrenched, which forces you to play very aggressively as the only way to win is to create an opening and break through their lines which requires sacrificing many of your own units.",
